=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The network is healthy and PC3's connectivity is fully intact. Exhaustive
end-to-end probing found no fault anywhere in the forwarding path. PC3
(10.3.0.100/24, VLAN 10) correctly reaches srv1 (Office B, VLAN 30,
10.5.0.4) with 0% packet loss, reaches pc2 in Office A (10.1.0.101) with
0% packet loss, and is reachable in the reverse direction from srv1 with
0% packet loss. PC3's ARP table has its default gateway (10.3.0.1 on
dswb1's br0.10 VLAN 10 interface) fully resolved.

On the access switch aswb2, the port facing PC3 (eth0) is in STP forwarding
state, carries VLAN 10 as its PVID with correct egress-untagged behaviour,
and the trunk links to dswb1 (eth1, forwarding/root) and dswb2 (eth2,
STP-blocked for redundancy) are operating normally. No iptables rules block
traffic on PC3 itself. OSPF-routed inter-VLAN paths through the distribution
layer (dswb1/dswb2) are working correctly.

A minor configuration asymmetry was observed: aswb2.eth0 allows VLAN 20 in
addition to VLAN 10, whereas other access ports (e.g. aswb3.eth0) carry only
their single data VLAN. VLAN 20 egresses tagged on that port and PC3, being
an untagged host, simply ignores those frames. There is no connectivity
impact.

The user's report that "the computer can't reach anything" is not supported
by any evidence found in the live lab. The complaint is a false premise —
the network is operating correctly and no corrective action is required.
